CloudBurrow patch 82 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1655).

The emulator served no profiles, so a freeze or a memory growth inside it
could be read only from a SIGQUIT dump, which ends the process and, with
it, every table the engine held in its temporary database. It now serves
the Go runtime's profiles (net/http/pprof) when
BIGQUERY_EMULATOR_DEBUG_PPROF names a loopback address, as CloudBurrow's
own processes do under CLOUDBURROW_DEBUG_PPROF (#1609), which the emulator's
supervisor reads and listens on itself. Off by default: with the variable
unset nothing listens, and an address that is not loopback is refused.

